Ladybird now converts a negative long long argument to the number that
was passed, as WebIDL’s ConvertToInt() requires. WebKit does the same in
its convertToInteger<IDLLongLong>(), Blink in its ToInt64(), and Gecko
in JS::ToInt64(), which its PrimitiveConversionTraits for int64_t call.
And the test’s output is the same, line for line, in Chrome 158,
Firefox 151, and WebKit 26.5.
